## Prerequisites & Environment Setup

Download and install Docker Desktop on your machine.
Open Docker Desktop and ensure the Docker engine daemon is running in the background.
Download and install VS Code (or your preferred code editor).
Download and install DBeaver Community Edition for database management.
Ensure Python 3.10+ and pip are installed on your system.

## Setting up local VS environment

Create a root directory for the project.
Open this root directory in VS Code.
create a new file named docker-compose.yml
Paste the infrastructure configuration for PostgreSQL, Apache Kafka, and Redis into the docker-compose.yml file and save it
Open a persistent terminal in VS Code using Ctrl + ~ (or Terminal > New Terminal).
Start the infrastructure services in the background by executing: docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up -d
Verify that all three containers (enterprise_postgres, enterprise_kafka, enterprise_redis) are actively running by executing: docker ps

## Installing Application Dependencies

Install the required Python client libraries for the architecture by running: pip install kafka-python redis faiss-cpu pinecone-client opentelemetry-api opentelemetry-sdk opentelemetry-instrumentation-fastapi

## Connecting to PostgreSQL (DBeaver)

Open DBeaver and create a new PostgreSQL database connection.
Configure the connection settings to match the Docker container:
Host: localhost
Port: 5432
Database: research_ai_db
Username: ai_user
Password: ai_password
Click Test Connection to confirm successful access to the local database container.
Click OK to save the connection profile
